# L §3.3 with L §7.3: with to, periodic(12 %/year, month, effective) is 1.12^(1/12) - 1 correctly rounded
# and printed with ≈ (not a rational on a cell edge).  Its digits are not asserted (L §7.3 values are checked by
# identities here); L §3.3's factor gives the identity: factor(r, 1, year, effective) = 1.12 exactly (round 6: over a
# year load shows the power t·n is an integer for an int n, so no to is needed).
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-12-31
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "s"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01

input r: rate
input n1: int
def p: num = periodic(r, month, effective) to 1e-9 at reader
def f: num = factor(r, n1, year, effective) at reader

version v
  cite s
  governs 2026..
  known 2026-01-01
  r = 12 %/year
  n1 = 1

ask a: p law 2026-06-30
ask b: f law 2026-06-30
=== expect
a: ≈ 0.0094 ...
  law date 2026-06-30, cut 2026-12-31
b: 1.12
  law date 2026-06-30, cut 2026-12-31
